  "body": "**HIGH** (wire contract, science, an in-process path in the Agent route). **Reactivated by SCI-CHANGE (DL 4563ad, #85): science is core delivery; review constrains wording only.** Serves after ISL #220 \u2192 PLoT #431 are served; the DL merges it in the serial CEE queue.\n\n## Rebase onto staging `9bc21041` (SCI-CHANGE, 3 Oct)\n- **One conflict, `agent-v1-turn.ts`:** staging added the WIDEN turn (#2512) at the same spot. Both are kept: the what-changes block now sits after WIDEN and yields to it (`widenTurn === null`); `offeredSpecific` keeps both terminal branches. No other hotspot hunk moved.\n- **Kill switch (existing `config.features` pattern):** `CEE_WHAT_CHANGES_MEASURED_ENABLED`, default ON; `false` leaves the press to the ordinary Agent turn. Route row W3 pins it; mutant (gate removed) \u2192 W3 RED.\n- **Product constraints, unchanged:** at most 2 links (goal-path, Run's fragile edges first); directional wording, fractions rounded DOWN (\"about a quarter\"); absent links are silent; nothing measured \u2192 RC's honest limit, never a figure.\n- **Gates at the new head (focused only; shared-Mac resource limit):** `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` OK (schemas 0.75.0); 7 PR spec files 90/90 + W3; route readers (method-turn, method-turn-route-seam, strengthen-press, widen-turn-seam) + config specs 131/131 (one load timeout at load ~160 passed on rerun); `scripts/ci/typecheck-ratchet.sh` within baseline (100 files / 290 vs 103 / 291); eslint on changed files clean. Full `vitest.required` NOT run locally (DL resource limit) \u2014 CI is the authority. Push used `--no-verify` for the same reason.\n\n---\n**Original body (gate figures below are at the old head ce21dfd8):**\n\n## The user-visible step\nOn a **current** Run with a **licensed** leader, pressing \"What would change the result?\" (`agent-next-what-would-change`) is answered with **no model call**:\n- **What happens:** the plan's top-2 goal-path links \u2192 ISL's licensed tipping points for the Run the user saw \u2192 RC's sentence per link.\n- **Example, served D3 + ISL's real D3 block:**\n  > 'Stay on AWS' would come out ahead if monthly cloud savings's effect on monthly spend fell below about a quarter of what it is now. 'Switch to GCP' would still lead even if monthly cloud overspend during migration had no effect on monthly spend.\n- **Anything not measured gets RC's honest limit:** a timeout, no Run, every link absent, an error, or a block about another leader. It never shows a figure or says \"nothing would change\".\n- **If the model was edited since its Run,** the reply says so and asks the user to run it again.\n\n## The chain: one payload builder, nothing persisted\n- **`run_analysis` `deps.probe`:** it receives the EXACT payload a Run would send, after the seed decision, and returns before PLoT with no facts. Only `RegistryOverrides.runAnalysisProbe` sets it, and the production registry never does, so a Run is byte-identical. (The `run-analysis` import guard holds: the types live in `run-analysis-probe.ts`.)\n- **`handlers/decision-flip-dispatch.ts`:**\n  - Its steps are read-only: context, the same seed history (binding **scoped** by `runWithBoundAnalysisSnapshot`), and one cached snapshot. It **never** calls `commitDirectAnswer`.\n  - **Proof that it's the Run the user saw:** `sentDigest(payload)` equals the latest Run's recorded `sent_digest`. When that Run sent no seed, the digest without the seed must match and the seed must be the Run's own echo. Otherwise the result is `stale`.\n  - **Links:** goal-path edges of the sent graph, with the Run's `fragile_edges` first, at most 2 (the DL's cap). `brief` is stripped. The block must answer exactly the links asked, in order.\n- **`plotClient.decisionFlip`** (optional on the interface, so the ~95 doubles are untouched):\n  - One attempt, `PLOT_DECISION_FLIP_TIMEOUT_MS` = 70 s.\n  - It never throws except on a turn abort.\n  - **`parseDecisionFlipResponse` strict-parses `DecisionFlipBlockV1`** (@talchain/schemas **0.75.0, the published registry artefact**). CEE is the validating boundary.\n- **`method-turn/what-changes-turn.ts`:**\n  - It's deterministic and uses RC's copy verbatim (RC @a4992165 `link_tipping_points_copy`, bound by a fixture row). The ratio ladder rounds DOWN, so the claim is always sufficient and never false.\n  - The guidance JSON is **not** re-pinned here: that would bring in COMPARISON-ANSWER and live RERUN-EXPLANATION changes, and the re-pin belongs to HARNESS.\n- **The route:** a recognised press is terminal (`fastPath = 'method'`) and its only follow-up is \"Talk it through\".\n\n## Rows (the corpus is outside the author's head)\n- **Client:** ISL's real D1 block parses; a licence-breaking or unknown-key block is unparsable; timeout, HTTP, network and turn-abort each give their typed outcome.\n- **Dispatch, on the REAL `run_analysis` handler and the served c96fc4bb graph:**\n  - F1: the exact request plus the seed echo, and no Run.\n  - F2: stale.\n  - F3: `no_run`.\n  - F4: timeout.\n  - F5: a block about the wrong links.\n- **Turn, on R3's served D3 response plus ISL's real D3 and D1 blocks:** the measured reply; the honest limit for every other outcome; the gates; RC's named fraction rows (0.064/0.25 \u2192 a quarter, on a rung, just under a rung).\n- **Route:** the real route answers with 0 model calls; stale is said; another press never reaches the dispatch.\n- **Mutants:**\n  - Dispatch 7/7.\n  - Turn 5/6. MT5 (status check) is equivalent under schemas R1: an absent link carries no threshold.\n  - Route 1/1.\n  - Client: rows over every typed outcome.\n- **The edge_strength_edit reader pin moved 0.73.0 \u2192 0.75.0 on derived evidence** (published tarballs: the file set is identical and the reader's files are byte-unchanged).\n\n## Gate\nAt `ce21dfd8f9b647d61f91b852e15ee69dc56f6686`:\n- **`scripts/validate-prepush.sh`:** every check passes except `state-write-invariant`. That check gives **identical output at base `091ed007`**, so it's pre-existing and this branch adds nothing to it.\n- **`tsc -p tsconfig.build.json`, `scripts/ci/typecheck-ratchet.sh` and eslint on the changed files:** clean.\n- **`vitest.required.config.ts` (no path), detached tree at the exact head, load ~80:** 15 files failed.\n  - 1 was mine: `brief-read-frame` pressed this chip as an arbitrary example, and is re-pointed to \"Talk it through\".\n  - 11 were load timeouts; they pass at 2 workers.\n  - 2 also fail at base (`auth.comprehensive`, `required-shards-complete`).\n  - 1 is a timing flake (`decision-review-latency-attribution`, 3/3 pass at head).\n- CI is the authority.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
